  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MENAfem school and convening</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MENAFem is a nascent and growing movement concerned with envisioning a new global economic system based on intersectional feminist principles, human rights, and ecological justice driven by the needs of communities and the marginalized, in particular in the Middle East and North Africa (MENA) region and beyond, and working to make it a reality. This project will draw on our expertise in IFIs/MDBs, debt, gender,and economic and climate justice, and their various intersections especially as they manifest in the MENA region,along with our experience in knowledge and movement building and collective advocacy.

The MENA Fem Annual Feminist Economics School presents a unique opportunity to address economic and ecological justice in the MENA region from a feminist perspective. Our aims for this project are to create a knowledge-sharing platform for feminist researchers, activists, and CSOs on the themes of the IFA reform, economic justice, and climate finance and justice in the MENA region

A group of feminist and allied organizations are convening a three-day gathering in Rabat, Morocco, in May 2025, to create space for strategizing, foster global linkages, and set a foundation for advocacy infused by global South feminist analysis, particularly from the MENA region. Offering space to grapple with the current geopolitical context of increasing militarism, fascism and anti-rights narratives and policies, as well as the continued erosion of multilateralism,this gathering will look towards the major policy moments in 2025, particularly the Fourth Conference on Financing for Development (FfDIV) and the 30th Conference of Parties (COP30) of the UNFCCC.</narrative>
  </description>
